---     Assemble

A simple command line utility to quickly check the assembled values of assembly expressions.

---     Installation

Run ``./installation.sh'' with sudo.

---     Usage

assemble {OPTIONS}

---     Options

        -a <format text>
                Replacing '\if' with the input argument and '\of' with the
                output argument set the assembler.
        -c
                Disable config loading
        -f <file>
                Reads input from file instead of user input.
        -h
                Opens help menu.
        -p <value>
                Sets the prefix for the file.
        -x (16 | 32 | 64)
                Sets $MODE.

---     Config

The config file is to be stored at $HOME/.assemble.config and in the case that
it does, the following values can be set:

        T_ASSEMBLER     Sets the value of -a
        PREFIX          Sets the value of -p

Note that $MODE may be used at any point in the config.
